/// How `upsert` and `delete` are materialised on disk.
///
/// * `merge-on-read` (the default) writes Iceberg v2 equality-delete files. Deletes are
///   applied at read time, so writes stay cheap and streaming-friendly, but only
///   catalog-native / Flink-world engines can read the result — engine-backed catalogs
///   such as Snowflake and the Databricks Unity Catalog cannot read equality deletes.
